<title>USA: N.Y Assembly passes NYC new bonding agency measure.</title>
<headline>N.Y Assembly passes NYC new bonding agency measure.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY, N.Y. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York State's Assembly Wednesday passed a bill that would create a new, temporary bonding authority for New York City.</p>
<p>The measure would allow the city to bypass a debt cap and sell up to $7.5 billion of bonds for infrastructure and other capital projects through the new authority.</p>
<p>The state Senate passed the measure earlier Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bill now goes to Gov. George Pataki, who is expected to sign it soon.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
